{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310800,"nonce":"Ik/g92tL/kQxB6Ot5qfdxGGI3Vg=","title":"2026-10-05 nbody \"no longer beats hxcpp\" = tiered target 484 vs llvm 362 on nuc; cause = LLVM GEP/TBAA maps keyed by IrId never cleared ...","message":"User (2026-10-05): \"nbody has been regressed for a while regardless of machine. It used to beat hxcpp.\" I had called it \"flat\" by comparing only to the previous CI run — WRONG framing; compare ratio to haxe-cpp and over a longer history.\n\n**Cause:** `gep_byte_offsets`/`gep_results` in llvm_jit_backend.rs (since bcad0a27, Aug 14) keyed by IrId, never reset per function. LLVM promotion (`compile_llvm_bead` -\u003e `compile_functions`) compiles main+callees in one backend, so stale entries from earlier functions stripped TBAA from advance's field accesses -\u003e mass reloaded 3x per pair, no SLP. Order/numbering dependent: 0a345d88 (branch-form array clamp) flipped it. Fix = clear both in `compile_function_body`. nuc A/B: tiered 484 -\u003e 362-372 (= llvm), other kernels ±0.6%. Gate 837-\u003e837.\n\n**Bisect method that worked:** CI artifacts expire (only ~11 runs kept; no history committed). Use the nuc: worktree `~/rz-bisect`, shared `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=~/rz-bisect-target`, `LLVM_SYS_211_PREFIX=/usr/lib/llvm-21` (repo .cargo/config points at homebrew), script `~/nbody_at.sh \u003ccommit\u003e` builds benchmark_runner (~75s warm) and runs `nbody --targets rayzor-llvm,rayzor-tiered,rayzor-cranelift --json`. `--single-target rayzor-X` for one target with stderr visible. nuc has no hxcpp.\n\n**CI runners are bimodal** (same \"EPYC 7763\" label): llvm/cpp 0.92 vs 1.01, tiered 1.07 vs 1.22 — compare within a mode.\n\n**Tools:** promoted-path IR is NOT dumped by RAYZOR_DUMP_LLVM_IR (only compile_all path); I patched a temporary dump after verify_and_optimize in compile_functions. `opt-21 -passes='default\u003cO3\u003e'` on the pre-opt dump reproduced the shape offline. perf on nuc: JIT addresses vs `RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS` regions tells Cranelift vs LLVM code.\n\n**Not the cause (deliberate):** LLVM calls haxe_math_sqrt at its runtime address (8df26dc0, store-forwarding rationale) — remaining gap vs hxcpp's sqrtsd may live there. llvm/cranelift drifted ~+5% since Aug (array OOB branch), not chased.\n\nRelated: [[bugs_array_clamp_regressed_nbody_and_method_values]], [[project_perf_deferred_until_conformance]], [[feedback_perf_measurement_protocol]]\n\n**Promotion memory (2026-10-05, user asked; ash fixed similar):** benchmark kernels promote ONCE each in warmup, ~10-15MB, 0.12-0.42s — not their bottleneck. Structural leaks exist (3d9e207: per-promotion `live.clone()` of all modules, leaked Context/backend, unbounded callee closure — ash d6f064e/2d490e0/bebe948 are the templates). BIGGER finding ab85ef3: `rayzor run` (Application preset) NEVER promotes — direct calls bypass record_call, main entered once, OSR variants only created by a promotion. `--stats` shows \"0 LLVM (P4)\". Sampler: nuc `~/run_mem.sh \u003cout\u003e \u003ccmd\u003e` / `~/promo_mem.sh`.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_nbody_tiered_tbaa_leak` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}